{%- comment -%}
  The design prints a short product code beside the title. A print-on-demand
  supplier's SKU is a 32-character machine string, which reads as noise in that
  slot, so only render a code short enough to be read as one. Merchants with
  real codes still get the design; Qikink's internal ids stay out of sight.

  Params: product, tag (p|div), class, brackets (default true)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign code = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | default: '' | strip -%}
{%- if code != blank and code.size <= 16 -%}
  {%- if brackets == false -%}
    {%- assign label = code -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- capture label -%}({{ code }}){%- endcapture -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if tag == 'div' -%}
    <div class="{{ class }}">{{ label }}</div>
  {%- else -%}
    <p class="{{ class }}">{{ label }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
